1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commits/18e275fecee5452648e824251822f0208e21ed41"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1724763?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kevwilliams","id":1724763,"login":"kevwilliams","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MjQ3NjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commits/0e3b4f32a8361220c57ba0730c9298c198871613/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T16:21:05Z","email":"kwilliams@datum.net","name":"Kevin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T16:21:05Z","email":"kwilliams@datum.net","name":"Kevin"},"message":"feat: Show consumer organization on service catalog tables\n\nThe Consumers and Approvals tables gain an Organization column ahead of\nthe project, show display names only, and drop the Consumer ID column.\nSearch still matches machine names and the consumer ID.\n\nBoth tables now ask the gateway only for this service''s consumers\n(metadata.name and canonical spec.serviceName), so it no longer\nenriches every consumer in the shared producer project. Approvals moves\nfrom the raw Milo list to the gateway query, which also means a 403 on\nthe list shows as an empty table rather than the IAM-pending message.\n\nThe generated GraphQL client is edited by hand: bun run graphql fails\nbecause @gqlts/cli pulls in a second copy of graphql.\n\nRequires the graphql-gateway serviceNames argument and ConsumerProject\norg fields to be deployed first.","tree":{"sha":"d76187bf34b5f9fd833d4ac4701fd01eadec91cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/git/trees/d76187bf34b5f9fd833d4ac4701fd01eadec91cf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/git/commits/0e3b4f32a8361220c57ba0730c9298c198871613","verification":{"payload":"tree d76187bf34b5f9fd833d4ac4701fd01eadec91cf\nparent f655f988498b8e1fd3d705366d5429ca624bdb0c\nauthor Kevin <kwilliams@datum.net> 1790180465 -0700\ncommitter Kevin <kwilliams@datum.net> 1790180465 -0700\n\nfeat: Show consumer organization on service catalog tables\n\nThe Consumers and Approvals tables gain an Organization column ahead of\nthe project, show display names only, and drop the Consumer ID column.\nSearch still matches machine names and the consumer ID.\n\nBoth tables now ask the gateway only for this service''s consumers\n(metadata.name and canonical spec.serviceName), so it no longer\nenriches every consumer in the shared producer project. Approvals moves\nfrom the raw Milo list to the gateway query, which also means a 403 on\nthe list shows as an empty table rather than the IAM-pending message.\n\nThe generated GraphQL client is edited by hand: bun run graphql fails\nbecause @gqlts/cli pulls in a second copy of graphql.\n\nRequires the graphql-gateway serviceNames argument and ConsumerProject\norg fields to be deployed first.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEb8FNfGdgytwOrlKr53J8QGQJ2j0FAmqz/HgACgkQ53J8QGQJ\n2j0unw//VgziSRQaljGc5AZGOg6pUOxPtZT21T2Vo8xYXxRDvqlE7efUGv+hdWyy\n6Ad56LirYnnatdQoSnogWbPqpyMQmcv8P7GQhEIxbcWO7kQP3EwnSSlUUBAbaGck\npdxg1V3ezPCgfNfDnk4mc+GtrDp/4LOhrPqIoUFJm2VxoxQDAGfFc5XsXIg6PMgq\noHR533BYaharr