 its root.","tree":{"sha":"6d947b675c56030a327fd88e28a1f6e6ef4cc6b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/git/trees/6d947b675c56030a327fd88e28a1f6e6ef4cc6b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/git/commits/23354bbfa3f55809eed4cdcb18b8f648e1fa3c68","verification":{"payload":"tree 6d947b675c56030a327fd88e28a1f6e6ef4cc6b5\nparent a6ef16de932eb8844c9b3d7f7bf15191cff4db3e\nauthor Kevin <kwilliams@datum.net> 1790094012 -0700\ncommitter Kevin <kwilliams@datum.net> 1790094012 -0700\n\nfix(test): update org detail smoke test for the rebuilt sub-nav rail\n\nThe rail moved off a literal <aside> onto datum-ui''s Sidebar\n(SidebarProvider/Sidebar), which renders divs instead -- this test''s\ncy.get(''aside'') stopped finding anything, failing CI. Targets\n[data-slot=\"sidebar\"] instead, the stable hook the component itself\nsets on its root.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEb8FNfGdgytwOrlKr53J8QGQJ2j0FAmqyqsIACgkQ53J8QGQJ\n2j3pphAAmcp2PK794Kst+8YmCioIKkLVQYXntu17c7X/6ZzNyqWIfr+9noA4jE6L\nuEHdINT1qJvmJwCPQ1ghE3+XKIOhGgMWsbu8dQJNUT9VGXviH5arFzz/MJ4FZ5vE\nS8SaMrAYVMqQBtTI02KDFP1m43IATu/lwWSX2/omImsWJ+sx438B5fV/ID+kdVwt\nQotzMMB9lsCemOF6wNCWiIRkODjOXd7nBcZR+bEDdb18IfV5Su//L5Q6Z+MDgsQG\nSkGL9ek9xAFl1BkX9kzW2ttLl4+PJVGYMQ+rcyQLzEaoRg4iky1CrU+XqWRpenw/\nCCg326dnztY2WIBF0X3SrU6uU9Of5Rix97Ws5gbd/1a/T6wiJ8eY0QI0cYkG3tKS\nddGHwXzEbUKsevNVqL7apcn8oISjaqCSkOafoq8l+h9s+DGpXrW5+J1o5notRV/b\nWziN4J44MhrzvXKAuDcIoOVpT6QkKBVvVUBtUB5U0pBh1VMq0kAdkuk90TMWQpLz\na7+an0ZtoXN4Uyzz/SfksBOVVdhmZVkCViN8NxTo1i9aQhpZtcxcbz7uKHaXXJGA\nJ/lMFkv3ehw01MZ5xuMBC4QlTOhr91pmhGynT5dmaCxXCZlqE4I3sZsWgYdYvWob\nlJxNGOIZNd1oyyVxiDMp2WDfPdgZmCmCYNKsKB/ndE5MQVbxhRo=\n=G5vT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T16:20:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1724763?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kevwilliams","id":1724763,"login":"kevwilliams","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MjQ3NjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commit/23354bbfa3f55809eed4cdcb18b8f648e1fa3c68","node_id":"C_kwDOOl0d89oAKDIzMzU0YmJmYTNmNTU4MDllZWQ0Y2RjYjE4YjhmNjQ4ZTFmYTNjNjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commit/a6ef16de932eb8844c9b3d7f7bf15191cff4db3e","sha":"a6ef16de932eb8844c9b3d7f7bf15191cff4db3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commits/a6ef16de932eb8844c9b3d7f7bf15191cff4db3e"}],"sha":"23354bbfa3f55809eed4cdcb18b8f648e1fa3c68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commits/23354bbfa3f55809eed4cdcb18b8f648e1fa3c68"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1724763?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kevwilliams","id":1724763,"login":"kevwilliams","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MjQ3NjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commits/a6ef16de932eb8844c9b3d7f7bf15191cff4db3e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T04:25:20Z","email":"kwilliams@datum.net","name":"Kevin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T04:25:20Z","email":"kwilliams@datum.net","name":"Kevin"},"message":"fix(nav): stop the active/hover rail item from shrinking to content width\n\nEvery nav row lost its full-width active/hover background as soon as\nit moved onto SidebarMenuButton: passing tooltip unconditionally makes\nit wrap the button in datum-ui''s Tooltip, whose outermost element is\n`<span class=\"relative inline-flex\">` -- a shrink-to-fit container.\nSidebarMenuButton''s own hidden={state !== ''collapsed'' || isMobile}\nonly suppresses the popup opening, not that wrapper''s layout, so the\nbutton''s own w-full had nothing definite to be 100% of and collapsed\nback down to icon+label width, expanded or not.\n\ntooltip only makes sense (and can only ever show, per that same\n`hidden` check) while the rail is collapsed anyway, so only pass it\nthen. SidebarMenuButton returns the button undecorated when tooltip is\nfalsy, so expanded rows skip the wrapper entirely and the background\nspans the rail again, matching cloud-portal.\n\nFound by pixel-comparing a staff-portal screenshot against\ncloud-portal''s own active nav item side by side.","tree":{"sha":"b61ddbdcc7456aa8de494b7b66bf0421c041e26b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/git/trees/b61ddbdcc7456aa8de494b7b66bf0421c041e26b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/git/commits/a6ef16de932eb8844c9b3d7f7bf15191cff4db3e","verification":{"payload":"tree b61ddbdcc7456aa8de494b7b66bf0421c041e26b\nparent 96583c711500427f1803b27bf98e0c5dd6201e99\nauthor Kevin <kwilliams@datum.net> 1790051120 -0700\ncommitter Kevin <kwilliams@datum.net> 1790051120 -0700\n\nfix(nav): stop the active/hover rail item from shrinking to content width\n\nEvery nav row lost its full-width active/hover background as soon as\nit moved onto SidebarMenuButton: passing tooltip unconditionally makes\nit wrap the button in datum-ui''s Tooltip, whose outermost element is\n`<span class=\"relative inline-flex\">` -- a shrink-to-fit container.\nSidebarMenuButton''s own hidden={state !== ''collapsed'' || isMobile}\nonly suppresses the popup opening, not that wrapper''s layout, so the\nbutton''s own w-full had nothing definite to be 100% of and collapsed\nback down to icon+label width, expanded or not.\n\ntooltip only makes sense (and can only ever show, per that same\n`hidden` check) while the rail is collapsed anyway, so only pass it\nthen. SidebarMenuButton returns the button undecorated when tooltip is\nfalsy, so expanded rows skip the wrapper entirely and the background\nspans the rail again, matching cloud-portal.\n\nFound by pixel-comparing a staff-portal screenshot against\ncloud-portal''s own active nav item side by side.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEb8FNfGdgytwOrlKr53J8QGQJ2j0FAmqyAzcACgkQ53J8QGQJ\n2j2HSg//ceF976gvZaeaBYT97SltRU+xMpkZyUpjzIyi8vsAWsC2hq3hKRnpH0XY\ntH99FnOgBh57BoUI2br1seLq/CVioLKud2EjAC8YCA9V8N2UD3vuyoREEzOhHW8J\nZvnQVCCtOXmQct7UKdiwhenv31tAzNKJs0aq9e0pU48YfPn7tV/aUbEIssuzpn5p\n3bN34dEMuwsl+dAVatFbAeJrHzHl78Ub+UgN9UX2W8fh/yM/ke8sGBK8yO+vEcGz\ncCWmXQ1/Gwyiwbm6Pj96KJd5Pp4LhM5Ko+auSLUxTMx7FdkJRBbvrAWPO9qtDr6m\nPiOXcvHQYI2sJp3auP0aufsYndevACguhfHgOhjzDYhJwKySzTyBnSe+S6oeeTFg\nT0ew1C2NUjKFJ09+Go8nJElX9/lqQqlml/eX0wf/Rgqk7FGeOPqBsL6XK3yNIo/K\nSogPYqZSXZ3uCn1BhgzhyIRkd3VcwxxMOnfxi4WS6uGUBXhjZjytMbizlZfHDmg+\nsYUbWECxXmjss8KI6awCHH3sv3f1512Uph3h7500pf2Txx1cLUoMIdnIt9j/z/h3\nBSCes1fUVamHXtck0VV13wInHGx9lLp67Nf2yUa98gxvzqFHPPWd0AnWoxZzkiId\nzCkenhkuzkozwZhnEdqKf4yNHfHVP79aHLX4QyRi9AEGQOJVHRo=\n=J5a5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T15:42:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1724763?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kevwilliams","id":1724763,"login":"kevwilliams","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MjQ3NjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commit/a6ef16de932eb8844c9b3d7f7bf15191cff4db3e","node_id":"C_kwDOOl0d89oAKGE2ZWYxNmRlOTMyZWI4ODQ0YzliM2Q3ZjdiZjE1MTkxY2ZmNGRiM2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commit/96583c711500427f1803b27bf98e0c5dd6201e99","sha":"96583c711500427f1803b27bf98e0c5dd6201e99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commits/96583c711500427f1803b27bf98e0c5dd6201e99"}],"sha":"a6ef16de932eb8844c9b3d7f7bf15191cff4db3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commits/a6ef16de932eb8844c9b3d7f7bf15191cff4db3e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1724763?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kevwilliams","id":1724763,"login":"kevwilliams","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MjQ3NjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commits/96583c711500427f1803b27bf98e0c5dd6201e99/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T04:17:24Z","email":"kwilliams@datum.net","name":"Kevin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T04:17:24Z","email":"kwilliams@datum.net","name":"Kevin"},"message":"feat(nav): animate the sub-nav rail''s collapse/expand and label fade\n\nPhase 4 of the sub-nav/cloud-portal parity plan (see\ndocs/local/subnav-parity-plan.md, gitignored). Ports cloud-portal''s\nmotion CSS into app/styles/root.css (this repo has one global\nstylesheet, not a separate custom.css): an eased 260ms curve on each\nnav row plus an asymmetric label fade (out fast with no delay so text\nnever lingers over a narrowing rail, in slightly slower after the panel\nhas begun widening), respecting prefers-reduced-motion. Also corrects a\nspacer/panel timing mismatch cloud-portal itself left in place.\n\nThis required actually restructuring the nav item, not just adding\nCSS: Phase 2 deliberately kept labels conditionally unmounted rather\nthan always-mounted + CSS-hidden, specifically because the CSS to make\nthat meaningful didn''t exist yet. This phase is what flips it -- labels\n(and a group''s adornments/chevron, bundled into the same trailing span\nso they fade together) are now always rendered. Group items needed a\nbigger change: their collapsed and expanded states used to render\ndifferent content entirely (icon-only link vs. icon+label+chevron\nbutton), not just different wrappers, so there was no label to fade in\nthe collapsed case. Extracted a single content block both branches\nshare; only the wrapper and click behavior still fork on collapsed\nstate, since collapsed-navigates vs. expanded-toggles is a real\nbehavioral difference.\n\nUpdates the one Cypress assertion this breaks\n(cy.contains(''Organizations'').should(''not.exist''), expecting the label\nto be unmounted) to assert the computed opacity directly, since\nCypress''s documented visibility algorithm doesn''t cover opacity as a\nvisibility signal.","tree":{"sha":"d64a6110f8d0c99cf579a94a463be44f5184bae0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/git/trees/d64a6110f8d0c99cf579a94a463be44f5184bae0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/git/commits/96583c711500427f1803b27bf98e0c5dd6201e99","verification":{"payload":"tree d64a6110f8d0c99cf579a94a463be44f5184bae0\nparent 5c7bd42f0026546ea603d47001abc2662d401ea8\nauthor Kevin <kwilliams@datum.net> 1790050644 -0700\ncommitter Kevin <kwilliams@datum.net> 1790050644 -0700\n\nfeat(nav): animate the sub-nav rail''s collapse/expand and label fade\n\nPhase 4 of the sub-nav/cloud-portal parity plan (see\ndocs/local/subnav-parity-plan.md, gitignored). Ports cloud-portal''s\nmotion CSS into app/styles/root.css (this repo has one global\nstylesheet, not a separate custom.css): an eased 260ms curve on each\nnav row plus an asymmetric label fade (out fast with no delay so text\nnever lingers over a narrowing rail, in slightly slower after the panel\nhas begun widening), respecting prefers-reduced-motion. Also corrects a\nspacer/panel timing mismatch cloud-portal itself left in place.\n\nThis required actually restructuring the nav item, not just adding\nCSS: Phase 2 deliberately kept labels conditionally unmounted rather\nthan always-mounted + CSS-hidden, specifically because the CSS to make\nthat meaningful didn''t exist yet. This phase is what flips it -- labels\n(and a group''s adornments/chevron, bundled into the same trailing span\nso they fade together) are now always rendered. Group items needed a\nbigger change: their collapsed and expanded states used to render\ndifferent content entirely (icon-only link vs. icon+label+chevron\nbutton), not just different wrappers, so there was no label to fade in\nthe collapsed case. Extracted a single content block both branches\nshare; only the wrapper and click behavior still fork on collapsed\nstate, since collapsed-navigates vs. expanded-toggles is a real\nbehavioral difference.\n\nUpdates the one Cypress assertion this breaks\n(cy.contains(''Organizations'').should(''not.exist''), expecting the label\nto be unmounted) to assert the computed opacity directly, since\nCypress''s documented visibility algorithm doesn''t cover opacity as a\nvisibility signal.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEb8FNfGdgytwOrlKr53J8QGQJ2j0FAmqyAVcACgkQ53J8QGQJ\n2j0UqA/+MBzWgadwbvbbSpLjbIuwJ0G/DlWHr1A7tbD8KQF64qFhoCiyyCiFnDkK\ntjdh+fZrZr6zPhthzqbeSxgXAlpcshHR31KrxHHz1Lp0QG42EznhPoogPbdAExft\n7yK6TxsUrsgVqZankdZBfdhbxppj+3qyV9ba/O5ef+xLsYX7XopzidRy+VKzfICP\nw9MmSO1tc/InUxH+lf8Jq0L7ZgPw7n4+1GzRI0XEqpjosBgUNk/njczOgAtZMeKQ\nmo5gjQmGpH7UaZF8G0qLhpy80xD7o+bXP1Fykw69i//RbzUQVUDeKEG8znKRlqZx\nrmrx11W0yZnSvD4P+C2TUWbjOjzf2HXP7hrvMmSN/qFEU9Vn7V1lcXjqYIsZA48t\nPRarrxogSsJS6spIp3BP8FB1lagFzDyaz8XLrqzr9/i6C9EgMmrulbYOZjJ3Fb47\nWoatFGrWA+itStIPtZfORcHIaxss0YmbLv51eCOlWX+eUgbyZkQBmtYX17a8ka2a\nSYdG31h0LqcoSLq0z+aDZLgOuy5gEsarotnugr+XcoPC9RqIKaRGVWqLwEJtrVlA\nwbRO+XtaIoKTISCuMFQwUzfRB3oUVVXILVSM+hFqaurKfJXG5jkTTGFcskHiuYmg\nGGYI39S65UJNOiOrikAQ9//ObilHd77mxr4sgwm+8jlPUbTtLIY=\n=lSa4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T15:42:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1724763?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kevwilliams","id":1724763,"login":"kevwilliams","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MjQ3NjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commit/96583c711500427f1803b27bf98e0c5dd6201e99","node_id":"C_kwDOOl0d89oAKDk2NTgzYzcxMTUwMDQyN2YxODAzYjI3YmY5OGUwYzVkZDYyMDFlOTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commit/5c7bd42f0026546ea603d47001abc2662d401ea8","sha":"5c7bd42f0026546ea603d47001abc2662d401ea8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commits/5c7bd42f0026546ea603d47001abc2662d401ea8"}],"sha":"96583c711500427f1803b27bf98e0c5dd6201e99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commits/96583c711500427f1803b27bf98e0c5dd6201e99"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1724763?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kevwilliams","id":1724763,"login":"kevwilliams","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MjQ3NjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commits/5c7bd42f0026546ea603d47001abc2662d401ea8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T01:56:50Z","email":"kwilliams@datum.net","name":"Kevin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T01:56:50Z","email":"kwilliams@datum.net","name":"Kevin"},"message":"feat(nav): collapsed sub-nav rail peeks on hover instead of staying pinned\n\nPhase 3 of the sub-nav/cloud-portal parity plan (see\ndocs/local/subnav-parity-plan.md, gitignored). Sets expandOnHover and\nties expandBehavior to the rail''s pin state (open=true -> push,\nreflowing content; unpinned -> overlay, so a hover-peek floats over the\npage instead). Hovering never touches the pin/cookie, since that''s\ndatum-ui''s internal isHovered state, separate from setOpen.\n\nAlso wires the same hover handlers onto the entity rail''s header\n(SidebarHeader has no built-in hover wiring the way\nSidebarContent/SidebarFooter do), so hovering exactly over the\nback-link/title area of a collapsed entity rail also triggers the peek.\n\nFixes a real, immediate stacking-order bug this surfaces: datum-ui ties\nthe rail''s overlay z-index to expandBehavior, not to whether it''s\nactually expanded, so an unpinned rail sits at z-50 at rest, not just\nwhile peeking. Bumps two concrete collision points that this actually\nreaches today: the list page filter toggle''s intentional -12px overhang\nonto the rail''s border, and the assistant panel''s full-width bottom\nsheet (previously z-40, now under the rail''s icon column at rest on\nany chatbot-enabled page with an unpinned rail -- the common case).\n\nHover behavior itself has no test coverage yet -- the existing Cypress\nspecs never trigger a real hover, so they''re unaffected but don''t\nexercise this.","tree":{"sha":"87e6a74154d6cac5923d07cc73d3a5db3d8eca54","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/git/trees/87e6a74154d6cac5923d07cc73d3a5db3d8eca54"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/git/commits/5c7bd42f0026546ea603d47001abc2662d401ea8","verification":{"payload":"tree 87e6a74154d6cac5923d07cc73d3a5db3d8eca54\nparent 05e75a2f4489611a40718fd31e0e8184add95e87\nauthor Kevin <kwilliams@datum.net> 1790042210 -0700\ncommitter Kevin <kwilliams@datum.net> 1790042210 -0700\n\nfeat(nav): collapsed sub-nav rail peeks on hover instead of staying pinned\n\nPhase 3 of the sub-nav/cloud-portal parity plan (see\ndocs/local/subnav-parity-plan.md, gitignored). Sets expandOnHover and\nties expandBehavior to the rail''s pin state (open=true -> push,\nreflowing content; unpinned -> overlay, so a hover-peek floats over the\npage instead). Hovering never touches the pin/cookie, since that''s\ndatum-ui''s internal isHovered state, separate from setOpen.\n\nAlso wires the same hover handlers onto the entity rail''s header\n(SidebarHeader has no built-in hover wiring the way\nSidebarContent/SidebarFooter do), so hovering exactly over the\nback-link/title area of a collapsed entity rail also triggers the peek.\n\nFixes a real, immediate stacking-order bug this surfaces: datum-ui ties\nthe rail''s overlay z-index to expandBehavior, not to whether it''s\nactually expanded, so an unpinned rail sits at z-50 at rest, not just\nwhile peeking. Bumps two concrete collision points that this actually\nreaches today: the list page filter toggle''s intentional -12px overhang\nonto the rail''s border, and the assistant panel''s full-width bottom\nsheet (previously z-40, now under the rail''s icon column at rest on\nany chatbot-enabled page with an unpinned rail -- the common case).\n\nHover behavior itself has no test coverage yet -- the existing Cypress\nspecs never trigger a real hover, so they''re unaffected but don''t\nexercise this.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEb8FNfGdgytwOrlKr53J8QGQJ2j0FAmqx4GQACgkQ53J8QGQJ\n2j1X7g/+IzBPsxvYnQlMnueNaw3YtOGYGv45wScGtiASDHJRc7VnE4HnUHHVpTqz\naljzVbeYphfhWwmknOGL0BGOIdHTcBx/Y4ql2j8yzCsOKivvaGllCYgse6rF6dud\nM4SynKINGh2lAiRHnK9A8Zw8FWcJy04hSkM7bZ8LECaG8mDLQiXClFl7gj6w/4UX\nPp8KN5pqhX0R6CIDBR+8aRUt8mEnAxnNYvXuKOQ3WjjfpRsLQiKROFF/t4qSKpCb\nPvu/mjcwsxHlIbX2iqQi+C8f9pr61hTrAhEwKyOoO6Zp5ixuBtsH1Q1eU2HUnY/3\nYjarAeIIJvQOAdLChXjKcjSNXUljqOlnrvGduTtKLX3za3GKifqdXVzpdIjxRNrD\n35nM7Llrz2iob+iF+OQh29vpLYpOO3CTFg12uP2k9A9ZLcPuX3rahD0ZwRd1vTDv\nsFxEGGxPZLrweuPnOw82JTNMOjC+iP740qOKSKHR9TUPbDqBzG2c1nC3WybWy9BO\n89WlgbWQRZgP3MIbTfRM7H1y1jz1n3PH9rRKuEAc06vqLVD1t0EgfMMzf0CkplH3\ni6GIEDBC5jPnNR00regurE9kDgKAOK409+IUC0TkDlMYV+LFYl+TSuhUHusaWh0s\nqOItnb40PXWoqqNmt3SrVyVafsfBdoCRcRNBmzrjs6poKmCO3NY=\n=f/fj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T15:42:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1724763?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kevwilliams","id":1724763,"login":"kevwilliams","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MjQ3NjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commit/5c7bd42f0026546ea603d47001abc2662d401ea8","node_id":"C_kwDOOl0d89oAKDVjN2JkNDJmMDAyNjU0NmVhNjAzZDQ3MDAxYWJjMjY2MmQ0MDFlYTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commit/05e75a2f4489611a40718fd31e0e8184add95e87","sha":"05e75a2f4489611a40718fd31e0e8184add95e87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commits/05e75a2f4489611a40718fd31e0e8184add95e87"}],"sha":"5c7bd42f0026546ea603d47001abc2662d401ea8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commits/5c7bd42f0026546ea603d47001abc2662d401ea8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1724763?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kevwilliams","id":1724763,"login":"kevwilliams","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MjQ3NjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commits/05e75a2f4489611a40718fd31e0e8184add95e87/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T01:33:26Z","email":"kwilliams@datum.net","name":"Kevin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T01:33:26Z","email":"kwilliams@datum.net","name":"Kevin"},"message":"feat(nav): rebuild the sub-nav rail on datum-ui''s Sidebar primitives\n\nPhase 2 of the sub-nav/cloud-portal parity plan (see\ndocs/local/subnav-parity-plan.md, gitignored). Moves MiloSubNav off its\nhand-rolled <aside> onto Sidebar/SidebarMenuButton/SidebarProvider,\nwhich is what actually buys the hover-peek and push/overlay behavior\nin later phases — those primitives already implement the spacer +\nfixed-panel split that behavior needs.\n\nEach MiloSubNav instance nests its own scoped SidebarProvider rather\nthan reusing milo.layout.tsx''s app-wide one: that provider turned out\nto have a real dependent after all (SubLayout''s menu renders\nSidebarMenuButton, which calls useSidebar() internally), so it isn''t\nsafe to repurpose for the rail.\n\nPer-nav open/collapsed defaults (D3/D4) had to move onto a controlled\nSidebarProvider now rather than in a later phase, since an uncontrolled\nprovider''s initial state can''t react to the active nav changing without\na remount. use-subnav-collapsed.ts is renamed to use-subnav-open.ts and\nshrinks accordingly — the provider itself now writes the sidebar_state\ncookie on every toggle, so the hook only resolves the initial value.\n\nLabels stay conditionally mounted rather than always-mounted +\nCSS-hidden for now: SidebarMenuButton has no built-in hide-on-collapse\nfor its own children, so that only pays off once the Phase 4 fade CSS\nlands to justify it. Hover/overlay behavior (Phase 3) and the motion\nCSS (Phase 4) are not part of this change.","tree":{"sha":"9bb638b68400800ecc628122aea32a64ffdfe5bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/git/trees/9bb638b68400800ecc628122aea32a64ffdfe5bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/git/commits/05e75a2f4489611a40718fd31e0e8184add95e87","verification":{"payload":"tree 9bb638b68400800ecc628122aea32a64ffdfe5bb\nparent 74b8f000d8345f93924f0225e0b2afa00fb5107d\nauthor Kevin <kwilliams@datum.net> 1790040806 -0700\ncommitter Kevin <kwilliams@datum.net> 1790040806 -0700\n\nfeat(nav): rebuild the sub-nav rail on datum-ui''s Sidebar primitives\n\nPhase 2 of the sub-nav/cloud-portal parity plan (see\ndocs/local/subnav-parity-plan.md, gitignored). Moves MiloSubNav off its\nhand-rolled <aside> onto Sidebar/SidebarMenuButton/SidebarProvider,\nwhich is what actually buys the hover-peek and push/overlay behavior\nin later phases — those primitives already implement the spacer +\nfixed-panel split that behavior needs.\n\nEach MiloSubNav instance nests its own scoped SidebarProvider rather\nthan reusing milo.layout.tsx''s app-wide one: that provider turned out\nto have a real dependent after all (SubLayout''s menu renders\nSidebarMenuButton, which calls useSidebar() internally), so it isn''t\nsafe to repurpose for the rail.\n\nPer-nav open/collapsed defaults (D3/D4) had to move onto a controlled\nSidebarProvider now rather than in a later phase, since an uncontrolled\nprovider''s initial state can''t react to the active nav changing without\na remount. use-subnav-collapsed.ts is renamed to use-subnav-open.ts and\nshrinks accordingly — the provider itself now writes the sidebar_state\ncookie on every toggle, so the hook only resolves the initial value.\n\nLabels stay conditionally mounted rather than always-mounted +\nCSS-hidden for now: SidebarMenuButton has no built-in hide-on-collapse\nfor its own children, so that only pays off once the Phase 4 fade CSS\nlands to justify it. Hover/overlay behavior (Phase 3) and the motion\nCSS (Phase 4) are not part of this change.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEb8FNfGdgytwOrlKr53J8QGQJ2j0FAmqx2u0ACgkQ53J8QGQJ\n2j1O4hAAhui8fC/c/JNYbzy3cRriGFb+ENflCCPY8qWg4UVH1JpdndhLY2P+FOv5\n/cJGeHL7NGT1NxoK+WZrJ4Favsu4qoP1xgOoOjOJ4Gjvq0q/L9Bqyy/pjOidGa6n\nGWFlRdY4BohnVze+BQpUR8J1T1YzHR7YwWiSXN1QsIR4cY22PuJHcpjLYcs+qxS/\n9HaeXjgA5sYXzHIWz2trw5jjT6sQXVQFF76R0+czlNOBxk3zOsr1KT31yimqqIQO\n0+vj8tyyFHgibFVHVI7fIVCCmleklYd0Z4VAt0IOPeqQQNmuqtNj+OsjK+cdJAVm\n5BV341KeisEhbnQW3UP3KSyrOiVnOwhce48E5N3ucpl/VfypwwEdjKefUIDGCf6u\n/iCUBssJ/SpPdZyMCeBLdAUQEgPfbFxtlnIvgBUVIYmp1pu8+agt6o05KWeoND64\n074TMXe7mrffg+S7lahrHQULsehz9+Ap0eHofxeYNgxblfkQV+jZ4JYKYvmsrQvO\nh5ZVjJx6wcsxg1lt23Zdxaxf9V4Tn4w/rHwfPgqaZ+aVpuAZJ/xQJf8hMUzzSMVI\nnUv4Ut6ClQU1TW32TMLw5NbeMrMHlaz5zDXH2fAe9rmKcj05tqQO9eHJOUReG2TS\njXwatXYWW3sw24FxFMW5CclG1uZXiMTgFP8vHjseI2Gf5RISEZg=\n=0Kvo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T15:42:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1724763?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kevwilliams","id":1724763,"login":"kevwilliams","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MjQ3NjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commit/05e75a2f4489611a40718fd31e0e8184add95e87","node_id":"C_kwDOOl0d89oAKDA1ZTc1YTJmNDQ4OTYxMWE0MDcxOGZkMzFlMGU4MTg0YWRkOTVlODc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commit/74b8f000d8345f93924f0225e0b2afa00fb5107d","sha":"74b8f000d8345f93924f0225e0b2afa00fb5107d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commits/74b8f000d8345f93924f0225e0b2afa00fb5107d"}],"sha":"05e75a2f4489611a40718fd31e0e8184add95e87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commits/05e75a2f4489611a40718fd31e0e8184add95e87"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1724763?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kevwilliams","id":1724763,"login":"kevwilliams","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MjQ3NjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commits/74b8f000d8345f93924f0225e0b2afa00fb5107d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T01:15:19Z","email":"kwilliams@datum.net","name":"Kevin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T01:15:19Z","email":"kwilliams@datum.net","name":"Kevin"},"message":"fix(nav): kill the sub-nav rail''s flash of the wrong collapsed state\n\nThe rail''s collapsed/expanded preference lived in localStorage, read in\na post-mount effect — every load briefly rendered the default state\nbefore correcting itself.\n\nMove the preference into a sidebar_state cookie, in the exact format\ndatum-ui''s own Sidebar component writes it, and resolve it server-side\nin the root loader so the first paint is already correct. Falls back to\na client-side cookie read when there''s no root loader in the tree (e.g.\nCypress component mounts).\n\nThis is Phase 0 (verification) + Phase 1 of the sub-nav/cloud-portal\nparity plan; see docs/local/subnav-parity-plan.md (gitignored).","tree":{"sha":"180771c5d4db5b130e9ff70b84adcc2632545302","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/git/trees/180771c5d4db5b130e9ff70b84adcc2632545302"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/git/commits/74b8f000d8345f93924f0225e0b2afa00fb5107d","verification":{"payload":"tree 180771c5d4db5b130e9ff70b84adcc2632545302\nparent 28aba53ce9e2fc4096820ead535f7f6cf523f2da\nauthor Kevin <kwilliams@datum.net> 1790039719 -0700\ncommitter Kevin <kwilliams@datum.net> 1790039719 -0700\n\nfix(nav): kill the sub-nav rail''s flash of the wrong collapsed state\n\nThe rail''s collapsed/expanded preference lived in localStorage, read in\na post-mount effect — every load briefly rendered the default state\nbefore correcting itself.\n\nMove the preference into a sidebar_state cookie, in the exact format\ndatum-ui''s own Sidebar component writes it, and resolve it server-side\nin the root loader so the first paint is already correct. Falls back to\na client-side cookie read when there''s no root loader in the tree (e.g.\nCypress component mounts).\n\nThis is Phase 0 (verification) + Phase 1 of the sub-nav/cloud-portal\nparity plan; see docs/local/subnav-parity-plan.md (gitignored).\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEb8FNfGdgytwOrlKr53J8QGQJ2j0FAmqx1q4ACgkQ53J8QGQJ\n2j2J5g/+MVXJUUFrQRlE/xwdDvedG9sRiBFFzPSFRQ3WCnAXqj72MM8tBgPyLPTA\nwQ2vDZk3