ps://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commit/0f6373ba2cfb0cc248c0a1048405150d84d4e11e","node_id":"C_kwDOOl0d89oAKDBmNjM3M2JhMmNmYjBjYzI0OGMwYTEwNDg0MDUxNTBkODRkNGUxMWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commit/60b2220bfba5e5641059e7c9a5a00d91663d6d8a","sha":"60b2220bfba5e5641059e7c9a5a00d91663d6d8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commits/60b2220bfba5e5641059e7c9a5a00d91663d6d8a"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commit/41895c1731f8c6d8e0099187ea1d132aff0c5267","sha":"41895c1731f8c6d8e0099187ea1d132aff0c5267","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commits/41895c1731f8c6d8e0099187ea1d132aff0c5267"}],"sha":"0f6373ba2cfb0cc248c0a1048405150d84d4e11e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commits/0f6373ba2cfb0cc248c0a1048405150d84d4e11e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1724763?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kevwilliams","id":1724763,"login":"kevwilliams","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MjQ3NjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/commits/41895c1731f8c6d8e0099187ea1d132aff0c5267/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T16:33:05Z","email":"kwilliams@datum.net","name":"Kevin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T16:33:05Z","email":"kwilliams@datum.net","name":"Kevin"},"message":"fix: entity rail inheriting a stale collapsed state from the section rail\n\nCI''s e2e run caught this (#676): visiting an org page after the\nCustomers list showed the entity rail collapsed to icon-only, hiding\nevery label including Overview.\n\nMiloShell renders <MiloSubNav nav={...}> at the same position/type\nwhether nav is a section''s subNav or an entity''s - a client-side\nnavigation between them re-renders MiloSubNav, it does not remount it.\nuseSubNavCollapsed''s useState(defaultCollapsed) only applies that\nargument on the very first mount; once mounted, it can''t tell that\ndefaultCollapsed changed (e.g. Customers'' true -> an entity''s D4 false)\non a later render, so the *first* rail shown to a fresh browser session\ndecided the collapsed state for every rail after it, section or entity.\n\nFixed by only keeping an *explicit* user preference in state (read from\nstorage, or set via the toggle button); absent one, collapsed now\nalways reflects the current defaultCollapsed argument, live.\n\nAdded a regression test that reproduces the exact shape of the bug -\none MiloSubNav instance switching from a collapsed section nav to an\nentity nav via a prop change, no remount - confirmed it fails against\nthe old hook and passes against the fix.\n\nVerified with typecheck, eslint, and cypress run --component (full\nsuite green).","tree":{"sha":"998c51e18b6237cf3ce4990ce095a4f222a61897","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/git/trees/998c51e18b6237cf3ce4990ce095a4f222a61897"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/staff-portal/git/commits/41895c1731f8c6d8e0099187ea1d132aff0c5267","verification":{"payload":"tree 998c51e18b6237cf3ce4990ce095a4f222a61897\nparent 7234410d7fe866f2b6201c847de988252f3c8c15\nauthor Kevin <kwilliams@datum.net> 1789835585 -0700\ncommitter Kevin <kwilliams@datum.net> 1789835585 -0700\n\nfix: entity rail inheriting a stale collapsed state from the section rail\n\nCI''s e2e run caught this (#676): visiting an org page after the\nCustomers list showed the entity rail collapsed to icon-only, hiding\nevery label including Overview.\n\nMiloShell renders <MiloSubNav nav={...}> at the same position/type\nwhether nav is a section''s subNav or an entity''s - a client-side\nnavigation between them re-renders MiloSubNav, it does not remount it.\nuseSubNavCollapsed''s useState(defaultCollapsed) only applies that\nargument on the very first mount; once mounted, it can''t tell that\ndefaultCollapsed changed (e.g. Customers'' true -> an entity''s D4 false)\non a later render, so the *first* rail shown to a fresh browser session\ndecided the collapsed state for every rail after it, section or entity.\n\nFixed by only keeping an *explicit* user preference in state (read from\nstorage, or set via the toggle button); absent one, collapsed now\nalways reflects the current defaultCollapsed argument, live.\n\nAdded a regression test that reproduces the exact shape of the bug -\none MiloSubNav instance switching from a collapsed section nav to an\nentity nav via a prop change, no remount - confirmed it fails against\nthe old hook and passes against the fix.\n\nVerified with typecheck, eslint, and cypress run --component (full\nsuite green).\